# Channel status

Channel: `matrix`
Status: available

The channel `matrix` is available.

This channel is used to communicate via the Matrix messenger protocol. Your
account is configured, your username is {username}.

In Matrix, there is no real concept of direct messages, everything happens
within rooms. To respond to someone, use the `room_id` from the incoming
message' metadata in your channel header.

The channel descriptor JSON object contains these keys:

- `type`: Always the literal `matrix`.
- `room_id`: (string) ID of the room.

Example channel header for outgoing messages:

```
channel:{{"type":"matrix","room_id":"!someroomid:example.org"}}
```

Incoming messages additionally have these keys:

- `room_name`: (string) Name of the room. May be `null` if the room has no
  name.
- `sender_id`: (string) ID of the message's sender.
- `sender_name`: (string) Display name of the message's sender. May be null if
  the sender has no display name.

Example channel metadata for incoming messages:

```
{{
  "type": "matrix",
  "room_id": "!someroomid:example.org",
  "room_name": "Example room",
  "sender_id": "@alice:example.org"
  "sender_name": "Alice"
}}
```
